# AI Gateway - environment variables (secrets and per-machine settings)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Usage: copy this file to `.env` and fill in the values you need.
#
#   cp .env.example .env            (PowerShell: Copy-Item .env.example .env)
#
# The gateway loads `./.env` at startup (current directory only - start it from
# the repo root), or a file of your choice via `--env-file <PATH>`. Rules:
#   - a variable already set in the real environment WINS over the file
#   - syntax: KEY=value, `export KEY=value`, # comments, KEY="quoted value"
#   - the startup log names the file loaded, never the values
#
# Changes to this file are picked up while the gateway runs (it is re-read when it
# changes, or on POST /admin/reload) - adding or rotating a key needs no restart.
# A variable set in your real environment still wins over this file.
#
# .env is gitignored. Never commit real values; keep this file placeholders-only.
#
# A provider only reads a key if its config entry names the variable:
#     providers:
#       openrouter:
#         api_key_env: OPENROUTER_API_KEY
# So the names below are conventions - if you rename one here, change
# `api_key_env` in config/gateway.yaml to match. A provider with no key set is
# reported unhealthy; the gateway itself still starts. Providers with no
# `api_key_env` (local llama.cpp, Ollama, vLLM) need no secret.
#
# Several keys for one provider: put them in the same variable, comma-separated
#     OPENROUTER_API_KEY=sk-or-aaa,sk-or-bbb
# Requests rotate across them and a key the provider rejects or rate-limits is
# skipped for a while, so free-tier limits are per key rather than per provider.

# ─── Provider API keys ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# OpenRouter (type: open_router)  https://openrouter.ai/keys
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=

# Google Gemini (type: gemini)  https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
GEMINI_API_KEY=

# Hugging Face Inference (type: hugging_face)  https://huggingface.co/settings/tokens
HF_API_KEY=

# Ollama Cloud (type: ollama_cloud)  https://ollama.com/settings/keys
OLLAMA_API_KEY=

# ─── Other OpenAI-compatible providers (optional) ────────────────────────────
# xAI, Venice, Featherless, or any generic OpenAI-compatible endpoint. There is
# no fixed variable name: pick one and reference it from that provider's
# `api_key_env` in config/gateway.yaml.
# XAI_API_KEY=
# VENICE_API_KEY=
# FEATHERLESS_API_KEY=

# ─── Telemetry database (contains a password) ────────────────────────────────
# PostgreSQL URL for telemetry and the /v1/analytics/* API. The variable name is
# set by telemetry.database_url_env (default DATABASE_URL); telemetry.database_url
# in the YAML takes precedence over it. If unset/unreachable, telemetry falls
# back to log-only and analytics endpoints return 503.
DATABASE_URL=postgres://user:password@127.0.0.1:5432/ai_gateway

# ─── Logging (not secret) ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Default: ai_gateway=info,tower_http=info
# RUST_LOG=ai_gateway=debug,tower_http=info

# ─── Frontend (not secret; used by frontend/, not the gateway binary) ────────
# Where the Next.js server-side proxy reaches the gateway.
# GATEWAY_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8999

# ─── Tests only (never needed to run the app) ────────────────────────────────
# Disposable Postgres for the DB-backed tests - NEVER point this at real data.
#   docker run --rm -d -e POSTGRES_PASSWORD=postgres -p 55432:5432 postgres:16
# AUDIT_DATABASE_URL=postgres://postgres:postgres@127.0.0.1:55432/postgres

# Opt-in live smoke tests (tests/live_provider_smoke_tests.rs). Each is skipped
# unless its trigger is set; the *_API_KEY variables above also trigger theirs.
# Cloud runs spend a few tokens. See COMMANDS.md section 4 for the full list.
# LIVE_LLAMA_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8080
# LIVE_OLLAMA_BASE_URL=http://localhost:11434
# LIVE_VLLM_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8000
# LIVE_GENERIC_BASE_URL=
# LIVE_GENERIC_API_KEY=
